    <node id="Page 4 - Continuation of Analog-to-Digital Signal Conversion (page_number)">
      <data key="d0">Page 4 - Continuation of Analog-to-Digital Signal Conversion (page_number)</data>
      <data key="d1">page_number</data>
      <data key="d2">This page marker denotes Page 4 of a technical document on signals. It sequentially follows Page 3, which introduced analog vs. digital signals and sampling. Page 4's content is inferred to continue and likely conclude the discussion on converting continuous analog signals to discrete digital signals, covering topics such as quantization, digital signal definition, and possibly the sampling theorem, forming a crucial part of the chapter's progression from analog to digital signal fundamentals.</data>
