    <node id="Binary Expansion for Analog-to-Digital Quantization (equation)">
      <data key="d0">Binary Expansion for Analog-to-Digital Quantization (equation)</data>
      <data key="d1">equation</data>
      <data key="d2">Equation (1.3) defines the decimal value D of an N-bit binary number, used to represent a quantized analog sample in an ADC. It quantizes the continuous amplitude into one of 2^N discrete levels, where each bit b_i is a binary digit. This formula underpins the relationship between bit depth, resolution, and quantization error in digital signal processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-713b2bab6050e468d17f2fd671a62d07</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770441798</data>
