    <node id="ADC Resolution">
      <data key="d0">ADC Resolution</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">ADC resolution refers to the fineness of the quantization, which improves as the number of bits N increases, providing more discrete levels (2^N).&lt;SEP&gt;ADC resolution is a trade-off concept related to analog-to-digital conversion that is discussed in the context surrounding Exercise 1.7.</data>
