    <node id="Analog-To-Digital Conversion (ADC)">
      <data key="d0">Analog-To-Digital Conversion (ADC)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Analog-to-digital conversion is a process that receives an analog signal at its input and outputs a corresponding N-bit digital representation.&lt;SEP&gt;Analog-to-digital conversion is the process of encoding continuous analog signal amplitudes into discrete digital codes, for which Equation 1.3 provides the mathematical basis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54adab7d992eb1e107a550b8bcd3fa85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-713b2bab6050e468d17f2fd671a62d07</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442035</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Binary Representation">
      <data key="d0">Binary Representation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Binary Representation is a concept related to how digital signals are encoded, potentially introduced in the document's discussion on digital signal fundamentals.&lt;SEP&gt;Binary representation is the method of expressing data using a base-2 numeral system, specifically mentioned in the context of ADC outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental topic discussed within the chapter, concerning the digital encoding of information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54adab7d992eb1e107a550b8bcd3fa85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5215ab1adb791fd95187d113e17a4b19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-442ee34c5a776cfa12564adbd3f829b8</data>
