    <node id="Decimal Equivalent D">
      <data key="d0">Decimal Equivalent D</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">D is the decimal (integer) output value representing the quantized amplitude of an analog signal sample in the binary expansion formula.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-713b2bab6050e468d17f2fd671a62d07</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Binary Digits b_i">
      <data key="d0">Binary Digits b_i</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">b_i are the individual binary digits (bits) with values of 0 or 1, where b_0 is the least significant bit and b_{N-1} is the most significant bit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-713b2bab6050e468d17f2fd671a62d07</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Number Of Bits N">
      <data key="d0">Number Of Bits N</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">N is the total number of bits used in the binary representation, determining the number of quantization levels (2^N).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-713b2bab6050e468d17f2fd671a62d07</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Binary Expansion Formula">
      <data key="d0">Binary Expansion Formula</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The binary expansion formula is the standard mathematical method for converting an N-bit binary number to its decimal equivalent, as exemplified by Equation 1.3.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-713b2bab6050e468d17f2fd671a62d07</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Place Values (Weights)">
      <data key="d0">Place Values (Weights)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Place values or weights are the powers of two (2^0, 2^1, ...) associated with each bit position in the binary expansion formula.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-713b2bab6050e468d17f2fd671a62d07</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Summation">
      <data key="d0">Summation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Summation is the mathematical operation used in Equation 1.3 to add together the weighted binary digits to compute the decimal value D.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-713b2bab6050e468d17f2fd671a62d07</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Exponentiation">
      <data key="d0">Exponentiation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Exponentiation is the mathematical operation of raising 2 to the power of the bit index, used to calculate the weight for each binary digit in Equation 1.3.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-713b2bab6050e468d17f2fd671a62d07</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
