    <node id="Image">
      <data key="d0">Image</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Image is a visual artifact, referenced by a specific file path, that serves as the primary object of analysis. It is subject to comprehensive analysis, including content and visual examination. The artifact's associated metadata, such as captions and other descriptive data, is also utilized in this analytical process. The visual content of the Image specifically represents signal data; descriptions indicate it contains a visual representation of a signal spectrum, depicting the variation of a binary digital signal over time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8f2228a703be8bef62ad5b8318bb5af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f29b22be08d23160846f4c3cac8f32cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba2ced186359c941c816e5e5eda762f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-480cc8d41c6788e0155f15c324b76647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-905f3d2f135d774def7cdb42035893ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ca6310ef4a9d4c86d66da037b22eaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2846e3e2abff26edef2b72a265a32e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f469fdb8dc12182ae82e11ccca8a78b</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442038</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Visual Analysis">
      <data key="d0">Visual Analysis</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Visual Analysis is a structured data object or output that contains metadata and analysis results for an image. Its primary purpose is to provide detailed, organized information about an image. The specific metadata fields consistently include the image's type, its file path, and its page index within a document. It also contains textual elements associated with the image, such as captions and footnotes, with some descriptions using the singular ("caption," "footnote") and others the plural ("captions," "footnotes"). Additionally, the object stores spatial data in the form of a bounding box, often specified as bounding box coordinates, which defines the image's location within a page. In summary, the Visual Analysis serves as a comprehensive container for both descriptive attributes and positional data pertaining to a digital image.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8f2228a703be8bef62ad5b8318bb5af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f29b22be08d23160846f4c3cac8f32cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba2ced186359c941c816e5e5eda762f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-480cc8d41c6788e0155f15c324b76647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff84b12278674a0234b8f4aeaf7eb163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03064d4dac64b3d4a2275ef8afe38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-905f3d2f135d774def7cdb42035893ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee9cc1a778c219c8048f09d3e7c84498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ca6310ef4a9d4c86d66da037b22eaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2846e3e2abff26edef2b72a265a32e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f469fdb8dc12182ae82e11ccca8a78b</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442040</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Image Path">
      <data key="d0">Image Path</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">An **Image Path** is a file system location that specifies where an image file is stored within a directory structure. It points to a specific image file, often for the purpose of content analysis. The path is a concrete address, such as $C:\RAG-Anything\output\RAG_test1\hybrid_auto\images\27fee27753aaae50c0c5df53e289c9d4b46ff8edad685080f1d7ec9a0789fecf.jpg$, $C:\RAG-Anything\output\RAG_test1\hybrid_auto\images\5b1683c55f9520c2c4e1ac6f285a0108e68b8f81d6015dee6fd190d6431ab2d1.jpg$, or $C:\RAG-Anything\output\RAG_test1\hybrid_auto\images\d6a61cb49a786b0077f38fea488ee44fe6fe2564b2465c2c4e414edeeacaadcf.jpg$. In essence, it is the file location of the image being accessed or analyzed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8f2228a703be8bef62ad5b8318bb5af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f29b22be08d23160846f4c3cac8f32cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba2ced186359c941c816e5e5eda762f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-480cc8d41c6788e0155f15c324b76647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff84b12278674a0234b8f4aeaf7eb163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03064d4dac64b3d4a2275ef8afe38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-905f3d2f135d774def7cdb42035893ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee9cc1a778c219c8048f09d3e7c84498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ca6310ef4a9d4c86d66da037b22eaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2846e3e2abff26edef2b72a265a32e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f469fdb8dc12182ae82e11ccca8a78b</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442042</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Captions">
      <data key="d0">Captions</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Captions are textual descriptions, labels, or explanatory text associated with an image. Their primary function is to describe the content of the image, often providing specific technical or contextual details. The descriptions provided illustrate that captions are used across various types of signals and diagrams in technical contexts. For example, they can describe specific waveforms, such as a sinusoidal voltage signal with defined amplitude, frequency, and angular frequency, or a symmetric square wave signal. Captions also identify images as spectra, such as the line spectrum of a periodic square wave, or as the signal spectrum of an arbitrary waveform referenced from another figure.

Furthermore, captions frequently include alphanumeric labels like "(a)" or "(b)" to distinguish between multiple images or panels. They are used to describe processes, such as the sampling of a continuous-time analog signal to obtain a discrete-time signal, and to detail the variation of signals over time, like a binary digital signal. Additionally, captions identify schematic representations, such as the block diagram of an analog-to-digital converter. In all cases, the caption serves to objectively convey the essential information or context of the associated visual element.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8f2228a703be8bef62ad5b8318bb5af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f29b22be08d23160846f4c3cac8f32cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba2ced186359c941c816e5e5eda762f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-480cc8d41c6788e0155f15c324b76647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff84b12278674a0234b8f4aeaf7eb163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03064d4dac64b3d4a2275ef8afe38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-905f3d2f135d774def7cdb42035893ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee9cc1a778c219c8048f09d3e7c84498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ca6310ef4a9d4c86d66da037b22eaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2846e3e2abff26edef2b72a265a32e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f469fdb8dc12182ae82e11ccca8a78b</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442042</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Page Index">
      <data key="d0">Page Index</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The Page Index is a numerical identifier that indicates the specific page location of an image or element within a larger document. It functions as a page number, specifying where the referenced content is found. The index can be represented in different ways; some descriptions refer to it as a standard page number (e.g., page 1, 2, or 3), while others specify that it is a numerical value within a document's internal sequence, which may be zero-based. For instance, examples show the Page Index with values of 0, 1, 2, and 3, reflecting these different numbering conventions. Its primary purpose is to provide a precise reference for locating an image's position in the document structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8f2228a703be8bef62ad5b8318bb5af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f29b22be08d23160846f4c3cac8f32cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba2ced186359c941c816e5e5eda762f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54adab7d992eb1e107a550b8bcd3fa85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-480cc8d41c6788e0155f15c324b76647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff84b12278674a0234b8f4aeaf7eb163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03064d4dac64b3d4a2275ef8afe38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ca6310ef4a9d4c86d66da037b22eaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2846e3e2abff26edef2b72a265a32e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f469fdb8dc12182ae82e11ccca8a78b</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442044</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Footnotes">
      <data key="d0">Footnotes</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Footnotes are a metadata field used to provide additional textual notes, references, or explanatory information associated with an image. In the context of the provided analyses, this field is consistently reported as containing no information. It is variously described as being empty, absent, or explicitly noted with values such as "None." Therefore, for the specific image in question, there are no supplementary footnotes available.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f29b22be08d23160846f4c3cac8f32cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba2ced186359c941c816e5e5eda762f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-480cc8d41c6788e0155f15c324b76647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03064d4dac64b3d4a2275ef8afe38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee9cc1a778c219c8048f09d3e7c84498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ca6310ef4a9d4c86d66da037b22eaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2846e3e2abff26edef2b72a265a32e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f469fdb8dc12182ae82e11ccca8a78b</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442044</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bounding Box">
      <data key="d0">Bounding Box</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A Bounding Box is a set of spatial coordinates that defines a rectangular region of interest. In the provided context, the term is used to describe two distinct types of spatial definitions within a document.

First, a Bounding Box most commonly defines the location of an entire image on a document page. It is specified by rectangular coordinates, such as [324, 172, 709, 314], [298, 650, 747, 797], [188, 84, 763, 276], and [268, 693, 759, 844], which mark where the image is positioned.

Second, a Bounding Box can also define a specific region of interest *within* an image itself, as indicated by coordinates like [293, 85, 476, 169] and [268, 499, 759, 657]. Furthermore, it can be applied to locate specific document elements, such as a page number, with coordinates like [887, 44, 902, 58]. In all cases, it serves as a precise method for identifying the spatial extent of an object.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8f2228a703be8bef62ad5b8318bb5af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f29b22be08d23160846f4c3cac8f32cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba2ced186359c941c816e5e5eda762f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54adab7d992eb1e107a550b8bcd3fa85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-480cc8d41c6788e0155f15c324b76647&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff84b12278674a0234b8f4aeaf7eb163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80e03064d4dac64b3d4a2275ef8afe38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ca6310ef4a9d4c86d66da037b22eaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2846e3e2abff26edef2b72a265a32e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f469fdb8dc12182ae82e11ccca8a78b</data>
      <data key="d4">RAG_test1.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1770442045</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <edge source="Sampling" target="Discrete-Time Signal">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
