    <edge source="Time-Domain Representation" target="Frequency-Domain Representation">
      <data key="d7">3.0</data>
      <data key="d8">These are two complementary methods for representing a signal; the time-domain shows amplitude vs. time, while the frequency-domain shows amplitude vs. frequency.&lt;SEP&gt;Signals are framed via dual representations: time-domain ($v_a(t)$) and frequency-domain ($V_a(\omega)$).&lt;SEP&gt;Time-domain and frequency-domain representations are two complementary ways of analyzing the same signal, connected by Fourier analysis.</data>
